   "anchor": "FFmpegVideoDecoder<LIBAV_VER>::DoDecode / the software CreateImage() call",
   "evidence": [
    "+      mPendingFrameTimes.AppendElement(",
    "+      int64_t pts = GetFramePts(mFrame);"
   ],
   "notes": "ff_h264_decoder has no FF_CODEC_CAP_SETS_FRAME_PROPS, so ffmpeg's generic layer (media/ffvpx/libavcodec/decode.c) stamps every frame it returns with the pts/pkt_dts/best_effort_timestamp of the MOST RECENTLY SENT packet, not the packet that produced that image; confirmed with a real build (MOZ_LOG) and confirmed identical on retail Firefox 159.0 Linux with the distro's own libavcodec.so.59, so this is a Mozilla-wrapper-level gap, not specific to our ffvpx. Pushes the real (time, duration) of every sample before avcodec_send_packet, pops the smallest pending time (not the oldest sent one: B-frame pts is not monotonic in send order) for the frame CreateImage() actually receives, instead of trusting GetFramePts(mFrame)/Duration(mFrame). Software CreateImage() path only.",
   "verifier": {
    "changed": [],
    "why": "Written directly from this branch's own diff against the Mozilla tag; no prior draft to correct."
   }
  },
